    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>UVDelta 06 isn't your typical local clinic: it's a structure entirely dedicated to veterinary emergencies in the Alpes-Maritimes, based at 386 route de la Baronne in Saint-Laurent-du-Var. The official website calls it "the only veterinary clinic in the Alpes-Maritimes dedicated solely to emergencies, resuscitation and intensive care", open at night, at weekends and on public holidays, 7 days a week. It also describes itself as a reference service to which vets across the PACA region entrust their emergencies.</p>

      <div class="callout" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><svg><use href="#i-alert"/></svg> Published hours: Monday to Friday 7pm-8am, from Saturday noon to Monday 8am, and on public holidays from the previous evening 7pm to the next morning 8am. No daytime opening on weekdays.</div>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>UVDelta 06 takes over from the department's regular vet clinics when they're closed: at night, on weekends and on public holidays. If your dog has a health issue during these times during your stay in the Alpes-Maritimes, this is the kind of structure to contact first, alongside your regular vet, who can also point you in the right direction.</p>
      <p>The emergency number shown on the website is 0 800 94 84 84 (free of charge). The website asks you to contact the service by phone for any emergency or medical request: call before heading over. The published email address is uvdelta@gmail.com; the service also has a Facebook page and an Instagram account.</p>
      <p>The website describes a team of emergency vets trained for all kinds of emergencies, from simple injuries to cases needing resuscitation and intensive care, with technical equipment and ongoing training specific to emergency work. No prices, payment methods or list of species are published: ask by phone.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Saint-Laurent-du-Var is a coastal town in the Alpes-Maritimes, between Nice and Cagnes-sur-Mer. The website gives no parking or access details: ask for directions by phone before setting out at night.</p>
